# Gender & City Monitoring API — client integration guide

This document is for the **admin web client** building gender-ratio and city-distribution dashboards.

Use this endpoint instead of `GET /api/admin/analytics/demographics` for gender monitoring. The demographics endpoint only filters by profile `createdAt` and does not expose the cohort filters, precomputed ratios, or trend series needed for daily monitoring.

**Related:** [`FRONTEND_ADMIN_API_CONTRACT.md`](./FRONTEND_ADMIN_API_CONTRACT.md) — admin auth, base URL, and shared conventions.

---

## Summary

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Endpoint | `GET /api/admin/analytics/gender-monitoring` |
| Auth | Admin Bearer JWT (`ROLE_ADMIN`) — same as other `/api/admin/analytics/*` routes |
| Purpose | Monitor male/female ratio and city distribution for onboarding-complete profiles |
| Default window | Last **30 days** (`start` omitted → `end - 30d`) |
| Deleted accounts | **Excluded** (`accountStatus != DELETED`) on every query |

---

## Endpoint

```
GET /api/admin/analytics/gender-monitoring
```

### Query parameters

| Param | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `start` | ISO-8601 instant | No | `end - 30 days` | Start of the analytics window (inclusive). Used for **trends** and **city distribution**. |
| `end` | ISO-8601 instant | No | `now` | End of the analytics window (exclusive). |
| `granularity` | `daily` \| `weekly` \| `monthly` | No | `daily` | Bucket size for `inflowTrend` and `cumulativeTrend`. Case-insensitive. |
| `cityLimit` | integer | No | `20` | Top N cities by total count; remaining cities roll into `"Other"`. Minimum effective value is `1`. |

### Example requests

```http
GET /api/admin/analytics/gender-monitoring
GET /api/admin/analytics/gender-monitoring?start=2026-08-01T00:00:00Z&end=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z
GET /api/admin/analytics/gender-monitoring?start=2026-08-01T00:00:00Z&end=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&granularity=weekly&cityLimit=15
```

### Validation

- `start` must be **before** `end`. Otherwise the API returns **400** with `"start must be before end"`.

---

## Critical: what uses the date range?

The response uses a **hybrid** date model. Misreading this is the most common integration mistake.

| Section | Scoped to `start`–`end`? | Filter / date field | What it represents |
|---------|---------------------------|---------------------|-------------------|
| `approved.snapshot` | **No** (all-time) | Onboarding complete + approved + not deleted | Current approved pool **right now** |
| `onboardingComplete.snapshot` | **No** (all-time) | Onboarding complete + not deleted (any profile status) | Current onboarded pool **right now** |
| `*.inflowTrend` | **Yes** | `onboardingCompletedAt` in `[start, end)` | New onboarding completions per bucket |
| `*.cumulativeTrend` | **Yes** (buckets) | Built from inflow + baseline before `start` | Pool size at end of each bucket |
| `onboardingComplete.byProfileStatus` | **No** (all-time) | Grouped by `profileStatus` | Current approved / pending / rejected split |
| `cityDistribution` | **Yes** | `createdAt` in `[start, end)` + approved + onboarded | Profiles **registered** in the window |

**Rule of thumb for the client:**

- **Headline KPI cards and pie charts** → use `snapshot` fields (not filtered by the selected date range).
- **Line charts and bar charts over time** → use `inflowTrend` or `cumulativeTrend` (filtered by the selected range).
- **City chart** → use `cityDistribution` (registered in the selected range).

