## Graph mapping reference

### 1. Headline KPI cards

**Data:** `approved.snapshot`

| Card | Field | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| Total approved users | `total` | All-time, not range-scoped |
| Female % | `femalePercent` | Primary metric to watch daily |
| Male:Female ratio | `maleToFemaleRatio` | Display as-is; show `"N/A"` when no females |
| Female count | `female` | Absolute number |

Optional secondary row from `onboardingComplete.snapshot` for comparison.

---

### 2. Pie / donut — current gender split

**Chart type:** Pie or donut (2–3 segments)

| Variant | Data source | Segments |
|---------|-------------|----------|
| Approved pool | `approved.snapshot` | `male`, `female`, `unknown` |
| All onboarded | `onboardingComplete.snapshot` | `male`, `female`, `unknown` |

**Tips:**

- Use `femalePercent` / `malePercent` for labels.
- Hide `unknown` slice if `unknown === 0`.
- Add subtitle: *"All-time current pool"* so users do not confuse with the date picker.

---

### 3. Line chart — female % trend (pool health)

**Chart type:** Line (single or dual series)

| Series | Data source | X-axis | Y-axis |
|--------|-------------|--------|--------|
| Approved pool female % | `approved.cumulativeTrend` | `bucket` | `femalePercent` |
| All onboarded female % | `onboardingComplete.cumulativeTrend` | `bucket` | `femalePercent` |

**Why cumulative, not inflow:** Cumulative shows the **overall pool ratio** at each point in time. Inflow only shows new signups per day and can be noisy with small female counts.

**Tips:**

- Show date range in chart title: `{start} – {end}`.
- Consider a reference line at a target female % if product has one.
- Tooltip: show `male`, `female`, `total` alongside `femalePercent`.

---

### 4. Stacked bar — daily new completions

**Chart type:** Stacked bar

| Data source | X-axis | Stacks |
|-------------|--------|--------|
| `approved.inflowTrend` | `bucket` | `male`, `female`, `unknown` |

**Why inflow:** Answers *"How many new approved users joined each day, and what was the gender mix?"*

**Tips:**

- Good for spotting days with zero female signups.
- Pair with the cumulative line chart: inflow = daily intake, cumulative = pool composition.

---

### 5. Stacked bar — profile status breakdown

**Chart type:** Stacked bar (horizontal works well)

**Data:** `onboardingComplete.byProfileStatus`

Transform for charting:

```typescript
const statuses = ["APPROVED", "PENDING", "REJECTED"];
const series = statuses
  .filter((s) => data.onboardingComplete.byProfileStatus[s])
  .map((s) => ({
    status: s,
    ...data.onboardingComplete.byProfileStatus[s],
  }));
```

| X-axis | Stacks |
|--------|--------|
| `status` | `male`, `female`, `unknown` |

**Subtitle:** *"All-time current breakdown"*

---

### 6. City distribution

**Chart type:** Horizontal stacked bar (recommended) or grouped bar

**Data:** `cityDistribution.cities`

| X-axis | Stacks | Sort |
|--------|--------|------|
| `city` | `male`, `female`, `unknown` | Already sorted by `total` desc from API |

**Tips:**

- Chart title should include the selected date range: *"Approved signups by city"*.
- `cityDistribution.total` is the denominator for "X% of signups in this window".
- Per-city share: `city.total / cityDistribution.total * 100`.
- `"Other"` aggregates cities outside top N; `"Unknown"` means profile had no city.
- Tooltip: show `femalePercent` per city to spot cities with better female intake.

