## `inflowTrend` vs `cumulativeTrend`

| Question | Use |
|----------|-----|
| What is the female % of our **entire approved pool** today? | `approved.snapshot.femalePercent` |
| How has the pool's female % **changed over the last 30 days**? | `approved.cumulativeTrend[].femalePercent` |
| How many **new** approved users joined each day? | `approved.inflowTrend[].total` |
| Was yesterday's intake mostly male? | `approved.inflowTrend` stacked bar |
| Which cities had approved signups this month? | `cityDistribution.cities` |

**Cumulative math (for client debugging):** Each `cumulativeTrend` point = all profiles with `onboardingCompletedAt < end of bucket`, plus cohort filters. The series starts from counts **before** `start` and adds each inflow bucket. That is why the last cumulative point's `femalePercent` may differ slightly from `snapshot.femalePercent` if profiles were approved/rejected or deleted after onboarding during the window.

